# into the portfolio.
/products/*  /portfolio  301
/products    /portfolio  301

# v1.4.0 — the featured-client case study folded into /portfolio.
# v1.27.0 — that route was deleted outright with the client rename, so this
# 301 is what keeps any old inbound link or stale index entry landing on a
# real page instead of a 404. Keep it.
/portfolio/elfia  /portfolio  301

# v1.30.0 — stable outbound short links for the group's brands. Anything we
# print, WhatsApp or put in a document links to /go/<code>, never straight to
# the far domain: if a brand ever moves, ONE line here redirects every link
# ever sent instead of leaving dead paper behind. The targets must match
# constants/brands.ts — tests/brands-guard.mjs fails the build if they drift.
# 302, not 301: a permanent redirect is cached by browsers forever, which is
# exactly what we do NOT want on a link whose destination may change.
/go/azone  https://azoneofficial.com      302
/go/elfia  https://elfiaofficialstore.my  302

# v1.71.0 - the digital business cards (Track V). A person's URL belongs to
# the person and follows them; a ROLE's URL belongs to the company and stays
# with the chair. Print /ceo on anything company-issued and it keeps working
# after the person behind it changes.
# 302 for the same reason as /go above: a 301 is cached by the browser
# forever, and a role does change hands.
# tests/business-cards.mjs fails the build if these drift from
# constants/team.ts.
/ceo  /farhan  302
/coo  /zoll    302
/cco  /izz     302
